# Standalone image for the ONE thing this project's own sandbox structurally
# cannot do: download a spaCy NER model. Everything else about the OpenPII
# French evaluation (regex, fr_detect.py's dictionary layer, scoring)
# already runs fine without Docker -- this image exists only to add the
# French NER condition (`fr-ner` / `full`) to evaluate_fr.py's results, so
# it can be compared against the dictionary-only numbers already measured
# and written up without it. Near-identical to Dockerfile.meddocan_ner,
# with only the model name and entrypoint script swapped.
#
# Why a SEPARATE French model, not just "unblock the existing English one":
# the OpenPII French sample's carrier text is French. Presidio's default
# AnalyzerEngine (used everywhere else in this project, see detect.py's own
# _get_analyzer()) loads an English spaCy model -- running it against
# French text would not error, but would silently produce near-zero real
# PERSON recall (an English NER model has no meaningful signal on French
# sentence structure), which would look like "NER doesn't help here" when
# the real story is "wrong model was loaded." fr_core_news_md is spaCy's
# medium French pipeline (~45MB, NER-capable with PER/LOC/ORG/MISC labels
# -- Presidio's built-in SpacyRecognizer maps "PER" -> PERSON automatically,
# same label-mapping logic it already uses for English "PERSON"/"PER" and
# Spanish "PER").
#
# Usage: don't build/run this by hand -- run run_fr_ner.sh from the repo
# (any working directory; it resolves paths itself). It builds this image,
# mounts the whole repo read-only at /app (so evaluate_fr.py sees your real
# src/, fr_detect.py, fr_ner.py, and staged OpenPII_FR_raw.jsonl exactly as
# they are locally), and tees results to a file.
FROM python:3.11-slim

WORKDIR /app

# Only what evaluate_fr.py + fr_ner.py actually need -- not the full
# requirements.txt (same reasoning as Dockerfile.meddocan_ner).
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir \
    presidio-analyzer \
    presidio-anonymizer \
    faker \
    pyahocorasick \
    spacy

# Real network access (this is the whole point of running in Docker rather
# than this project's own sandbox) -- downloads spaCy's medium French
# pipeline directly from spaCy's own model release, not from this project's
# blocked huggingface.co/github.com allowlist gap.
RUN python -m spacy download fr_core_news_md

# Source and validation code are mounted at runtime (see run_fr_ner.sh)
# rather than baked into the image, so local edits to fr_detect.py /
# evaluate_fr.py / fr_ner.py are picked up without a rebuild.
CMD ["python", "/app/validation/real_data/evaluate_fr.py", "--with-ner"]
